}
```

Here's what each property does:

- `filter: drop-shadow(15px 15px 15px gray) brightness(1.1);` adds a drop shadow with some blurriness (the `blur-radius`) and darkens the image slightly using `brightness`. This gives the impression of light hitting the object from below.
- `transform: perspective(500px) rotateY(-25deg) translateZ(100px);` adds some 3D effects by rotating the circle around its vertical axis (-25 degrees in this case), as well as translating it along the Z axis (100px away from the viewer). The `perspective` property sets up a virtual camera looking at the scene, which affects how the rotation and translation look.

Feel free to adjust the values of these properties to achieve the desired effect! You may also want to experiment with different lighting angles and distances to get a better sense of depth. Let me know if you have any other questions!

