Next, open Visual Studio Code and create a new project. Go to File > Open Folder and select an empty directory where you want to save your project. In my case, I created a folder named react-app and opened it in VS Code.

Step 2: Initializing the project

Run the following command in your terminal or command prompt:

```sh
npx create-react-app my-app
cd my-app
```

Replace `my-app` with the name of your project. This command creates a new React app with some pre-configured files and dependencies.

Step 3: Installing necessary packages

We need to install two packages - axios for making HTTP requests and sweetalert2 for displaying alerts and notifications. Run the following commands:

```sh
npm install axios
npm install --save sweetalert2
```

Step 4: Creating the basic structure

Create a new file called `App.js` under the `src` directory. This file contains the main component of our app. Copy and paste the following code into this file:

