8. Add your desired JavaScript code to `script.js`.

9. Finally, open Google Chrome and go to `chrome://extensions/`. Enable Developer Mode and then click the 'Load Unpacked Extension' button. Select the root directory of your project.

10. Go to any website and you should see your browser action icon in the toolbar. Click it to inject the JavaScript code into the webpage.

