Assuming you have already established the database connection using the provided PHP code, here's an example of how to create a new socket for a specific chatroom:

First, you'll need to retrieve the necessary information from your database. Let's say the user ID and chatroom ID are passed as parameters to this function.

```php
function createSocket($userId, $chatroomId) {
    // Connect to the WebSocket server
    $websocketUrl = "ws://localhost:8080";
    $socket = new Ratchet\Client\WebSocket($websocketUrl);

    // Set up event listeners
    $socket->onOpen = function ($conn) use ($userId, $chatroomId) {
        // Send initial message to join the chatroom
        $message = [
            "type" => "join",
            "userId" => $userId,
            "chatroomId" => $chatroomId
        ];
        $conn->send(json_encode($message));
    };

    // Listen for incoming messages
    $socket->onMessage = function ($msg) use ($userId) {
        // Parse the JSON message
        $data = json_decode($msg, true);

        // Handle different message types
        switch ($data["type"]) {
            case "message":
                // Broadcast the message to all connected users
                broadcastMessage($data["chatroomId"], $data["senderId"], $data["message"]);
                break;
            case "system":
                // Handle system messages
                break;
            default:
                // Ignore unknown message types
                break;
        }
    };

    // Attempt to connect to the WebSocket server
    try {
        $socket->connect();
    } catch (\Ratchet\ConnectionInterruptedException $e) {
